# Negative control — makes every form take the engine's `reset` control,
# whatever its host. A dialog's "Cancel" then renders `type="reset"` again:
# pressing it empties the fields and leaves the dialog standing, with only the
# X to close it. The FE walkthrough defect 8, found on "Add new address" and
# true of all 36 of the registry's dialog forms.
#
# Intended RED:
#   a form in a dialog dismisses instead of resetting >
#     renders Cancel as a plain button, so it cannot empty the fields
#     emits cancel when pressed, and carries no verb with it
#
# The PAGE case stays green, which is the half that must not regress: the
# billing-settings form needs reset, so a fix that dismissed everywhere would
# be just as wrong.

